  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.5.12: IJSReadStream - a Stream whose data can be read while staying in JS (returned as a Uint8Array, no .NET copy). Lets a consumer that hands data back to JS (e.g. uploading model weights to a GPU buffer via IBrowserMemoryBuffer.CopyFromJS) keep it JS-side end to end. Includes a CanReadSync flag (false on async-only JS-backed streams like Blob in Blazor WASM). Implemented on BlobStream (CanReadSync=false) and ArrayBufferStream (CanReadSync=true). v3.5.11: HeapView support for ReadOnlyMemory and ArraySegment",
